# release-gate

A deterministic policy endpoint for CI container release decisions.

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm start          # starts on http://localhost:3000
npm test           # runs the offline policy test suite
```

## Deploy to Render

1. Push this folder to a **public** GitHub repo.
2. In Render: **New → Web Service**, connect the repo.
3. Build command: `npm install`
4. Start command: `npm start`
5. Render sets `PORT` automatically — the server already reads `process.env.PORT`.
6. Your endpoint will be `https://<your-service>.onrender.com/release-gate`.

## GitHub Actions evidence

`.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` is named exactly `TDS GA7 Release Gate`,
runs on push to `main`, has a step named exactly
`TDS identity: 24f3003125@ds.study.iitm.ac.in`, and runs the test suite
against the policy logic. Push to `main` once so the badge goes green, then
submit the **workflow page URL**, e.g.:

```
https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>/actions/workflows/release-gate.yml
```
